WEBVTT


00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.940
South Korea and Japan are right next to each other,

00:00:02.941 --> 00:00:05.321
but their cultures are completely different.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.360
Here are five shocking differences.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.600
First, the language barrier.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.740
They look close and sound similar,

00:00:12.741 --> 00:00:15.621
but zero words are mutually intelligible.

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:18.121
Second, cash versus card.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.200
While Japan still heavily relies on cash and coin changes,

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.780
Korea is a hyper connected card and mobile pay society.

00:00:25.781 --> 00:00:28.601
Third, automatic taxi doors.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.500
In Japan, taxi doors open and close automatically by the driver,

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.521
so never try to force them open.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.000
Fourth, public manners on trains.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.540
Koreans love talking and making phone calls on subways,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.161
but Japanese trains are completely silent.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.600
Fifth, ordering via tablet.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.420
In Korea, almost every restaurant uses touch screens and table orders,

00:00:50.421 --> 00:00:53.321
while Japan still loves ticket vending machines.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.020
Which culture shock is the most surprising to you?

00:00:56.021 --> 00:00:57.521
Let me know in the comments.
